<div class="byline">Adina Margineantu · August 2026</div>
</header>
<div class="intro">
<p>
    The table below lists proposed pulsar–supernova remnant associations. Columns, left to right:
    pulsar name, supernova remnant (SNR) name, normalized offset from the SNR center (β), age of the pulsar/SNR (kyr),
    distance to the pulsar/SNR (kpc), transverse velocity of the pulsar (km/s), pulsar period (s), the
    references for the association, and evaluation. 
   Evaluations are classified as Likely for associations with a significant amount of supporting evidence, Uncertain for associations that have minimal evidence, and New candidate for associations not in previous literature. </p>
<div class="legend">
    Transverse velocities marked with * are estimated from age, distance, and angular separation.
    Distances marked with * are estimated from Galactic SNR density and distance/size distributions.
  </div>
